# B0 (plans/backlog/BEND_LAWS_AND_AGENT_LOOP_LESSONS.md §A1): `--deny` names
# the outcomes that fail a run, and an unknown name must be a usage error that
# LISTS the vocabulary rather than being silently ignored — a typo'd deny list
# that quietly denies nothing is exactly the "green because nothing was
# checked" failure the flag exists to prevent.
#
# This case is deliberately solver-free: the deny list is validated while the
# option loop runs, before any file is loaded or Z3 resolved, so it asserts a
# real CLI contract on a machine with no solver. The rc behavior of `--strict`
# itself needs obligations and therefore a solver, so it is gated in CI's
# `verify` job (which installs the pinned Z3) and by the hermetic unit tests in
# tests/internal/verifier.test.yo.
stdout_keep_match=--deny does not know the outcome .*
